{"url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/chem/programmes/research-postgraduate-programme", "final_url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/en/chem/programmes/research-postgraduate-programme", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Home\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nPeople\nResearch\nStudents\nAlumni\nEvents\nUseful Links\nContact Us\nQuick Links\nHome Programmes Research Postgraduate Programme\nUndergraduate Programmes\nMaster's Programme\nResearch Postgraduate Programme\nResearch Postgraduate Programme\nMaster of Philosophy (MPhil)\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD)\nProgramme Highlights\nWhy Study Here\nThe Department is very unique in a multidisciplinary nature by integrating Chemistry, Biology and Environmental Science. Staff of the Department have a broad range of research interests include Synthetic Chemistry, Materials Chemistry, Biological Chemistry, Computational Chemistry and Environmental Chemistry. With a wealth of talent and a dedication to applied research, students can conduct advanced research and study under supervision of our faculty members who are actively working in their respective research areas.\nAims\nThis programme aims to train and produce graduates with an understanding of advanced developments and highly marketable specialist skills in the disciplines of chemistry, biology and environmental science, and to meet local and regional requirements in the industrial, commercial, government or education sectors.\nProgramme Intended Learning Outcomes (PILOs)\nUpon successful completion of this Programme, students should be able to:\ndevelop intellectual competence necessary to successful academic and professional work;\ncontribute to the generation and development of knowledge in their respective fields through independent, original, and innovative research;\ndemonstrate specialist subject knowledge and a high level of transferable skills with an emphasis on discovery-based element.\nProgramme Information\nProgramme Curriculum\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD) (admitted 2023-24 and thereafter)\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD) (admitted 2020-21 and thereafter)\nDoctor of Philosophy (PhD) (admitted 2019-2020 and thereafter)\nMaster of Philosophy (MPhil) (admitted 2020-2021 and thereafter)\nProgramme Requirements\nCoursework Requirements\nMPhil Students required to take 7 credit units (including at least 2 credit units of research methodology and ethics course at postgraduate level).\nPhD Students are required to fulfill the following course requirements within their study period:\n14 credit units (including at least 9 credit units of core courses and at least 2 credit units of research methodology and ethics course at postgraduate level)\n1 credit unit compulsory course (SG8001 Teaching Students: First Steps)\nTraining on Research Integrity (CITI Programme)\nQualifying Examination (QE)\nPhD students are required to take and pass a written qualifying examination in compliance to the regulations or guidelines as set by the Chow Yei Ching School of Graduate Studies (SGS). The QE aims to test students\u2019 knowledge of major subject area and assess their readiness to conduct research in their specific research discipline.\nQualifying/Annual Report Submission\nStudents are required to submit qualifying report and annual report in compliance to the regulations or guidelines as set by the Chow Yei Ching School of Graduate Studies (SGS). Such regulations and guidelines are accessible via the guidebook located at SGS website.\nThesis\nA MPhil thesis should present the results of research investigation, give evidence of a sound understanding of the area of study, its context and applicability, and make a contribution to knowledge.\nA PhD thesis, in addition to the above, should make a substantial original contribution to knowledge in the subject area concerned.\nPublication\nCHEM PhD Students admitted in 2023/24 and thereafter are required to have at least 1 first-author or co-first author paper published/accepted for publication/submitted for review (with proof) upon graduation.\nCourse List\nCourse List\nAdmission\nAdmission Requirements\nApplicants should satisfy the following minimum entrance requirements:\nMPhil:\nhold a relevant bachelor\u2019s degree with first or second class honours (or equivalent qualification) from a recognized university.\nPhD:\nhold a bachelor\u2019s degree with first class honours (or equivalent qualification) from a recognized university;\nhold a master\u2019s degree (or equivalent qualification) from a recognized university;\nhold a higher degree by research (for equivalent qualification) from a recognized university; or\nbe a current MPhil student in the University who seeks transfer to PhD Candidature.\nApplication Procedures\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS)\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS) is a highly prestigious award established by the Research Grants Council (RGC) of the HKSAR Government. The Scheme aims to attract the best and talented students all over the world to pursue their research degree programmes in Hong Kong\u2019s institutions. Students graduated or graduating with a bachelor or master degree with good academic records and experience are invited to apply. For application procedures and details, please click here.\nNormal Round Application\nFor application procedures and details, please click here.\nAPPLY NOW\nPeriod of Study\nProgramme of Study Full-time Part-time\nMPhil 2 years 4 years\nPhD 4 years 8 years\nTuition Fee\nPlease click here.\nYour Potential Supervisor\nYour Potential Supervisor\nAbout Us\nWelcome Message\nIntroduction\nAwards & Achievements\nNotable Scholars\nFacts & Figures\nNews\nOur Videos\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate Programmes\nMaster's Programme\nResearch Postgraduate Programme\nPeople\nAcademic Staff\nAdministrative Staff\nTechnical Staff\nResearch Staff\nResearch Students\nResearch\nGrants Awarded\nSelected Publications\nResearch Areas\nResearch Centres\nFacilities & Equipment (for staff & student